# mindone - intentionally empty.
#
# 07.09: there used to be two lines here, `typeattribute proc_battery_cmd proc_type;` and `typeattribute proc_aed
# proc_type;`, added from the A16 log audit (par. 4.5). They were needed for REPACKAGING, where we
# patch the already-compiled stock policy via CIL (`sepolicy/repack-extra.cil`): in the device's binary
# policy these types really did lack the `proc_type` attribute, hence the "associate" denial.
#
# In a build from source they must not be here, and they break the build:
#   file.te:3:ERROR 'unknown type proc_battery_cmd'  ->  vendor_sepolicy.cil fails to compile.
# Reason: both types are ALREADY declared with the needed attribute in the MediaTek policy -
#   device/mediatek/sepolicy_vndr/base/private/file.te:25   type proc_battery_cmd, fs_type, proc_type;
#   device/mediatek/sepolicy_vndr/debug/vendor/file.te:24   type proc_aed, fs_type, proc_type;
# and the first one is in `private`, meaning the vendor policy cannot see it at all, so a repeated
# `typeattribute` for it references an unknown type.
#
# 🔴 Rule for the future: fixes devised for CIL repair of a binary policy do NOT carry over
# into the source tree one-to-one - always check first how the type is declared in the sources.
#
# The file is kept (not deleted) on purpose: deleting it changes the file list under the
# `sepolicy/vendor/*.te` glob and forces soong to redo its analysis (F3834), whereas editing the content does not.

# mindone 09.09 (F4059): a type of OUR OWN for fingerprint data is NOT needed - it is already declared in AOSP
# (system/sepolicy/public/file.te:535, `type fingerprint_vendor_data_file, file_type,
# data_file_type;`), which also labels the path /data/vendor_de/<user>/fpdata. Our Silead blob puts
# its config in /data/vendor/silead, so only a label (file_contexts) and rules
# (hal_fingerprint_default.te) are needed. Declaring our own type with the same name would break the
# full build with a name conflict - caught by the check before flashing.

# Camera flip-module hall switch position exported by our mtk_kpd driver
# (/sys/devices/platform/soc/10010000.kp/hall_position); read once at boot by the
# MindOneKeyHandler inside system_server (CAMERA-FLIP-PLAN-1309).
type sysfs_mindone_hall, fs_type, sysfs_type;
